<section class="bhd-page__feature" id="why-glucose" data-lp-section="mechanism">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">THE MECHANISM</p>
    <h2>Glucose has a job.</h2>
    <p>Sodium and glucose can be transported together in the small intestine. Water follows absorbed solutes, which is why glucose has a functional role in oral hydration physiology.</p>
    <p><strong>The goal is not maximum sugar. It is purposeful glucose in a low-sugar formula.</strong></p>
  </div>
</section>

